{"name":"Witch Wood","hex":"#7c4a33","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"witch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person (now usually particularly a woman) who uses magical or supernatural powers to influence or predict events, particularly one with malicious motives.\n\n A person of any gender who harmfully employs magical power (especially innate rather than ritual)","A person of any gender who harmfully employs magical power (especially innate rather than ritual)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To dowse for water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/witch"},{"term":"wood","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The substance making up the central part of the trunk and branches of a tree. Used as a material for construction, to manufacture various items, etc. or as fuel.","The wood from a particular species of tree."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover or plant with trees.","To hide behind trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wood"}],"entries":[{"title":"Witch Wood","blocks":[{"text":"Witch Wood is a 1927 historical novel by the Scottish author John Buchan, set in the Scottish Borders during the 17th-century Wars of the Three Kingdoms. It follows the story of a young Church of Scotland minister, newly-arrived in a rural parish, who is undermined by devil-worshipping parishioners. A substantial part of the dialogue is in Scots."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ef/Witch_wood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Witch_Wood","wikidata":"Q8027856"},{"title":"Witchcraft","blocks":[{"text":"Witchcraft is the use of magic by a person called a witch. Traditionally, \"witchcraft\" means the use of magic to inflict supernatural harm or misfortune on others, and this remains the most common and widespread meaning. Though the idea of witchcraft is largely imaginary, it has nevertheless served in many cultures as a way to explain the presence of evil. The belief in witches has been found throughout history in a great number of societies worldwide. Most of these societies have used protective magic or counter-magic against witchcraft, and have shunned, banished, imprisoned, physically punished or killed alleged witches. Anthropologists use the term \"witchcraft\" for similar beliefs about harmful occult practices in different cultures, and these societies often use the term when speaking in English."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/John_William_Waterhouse_-_Magic_Circle.JPG/330px-John_William_Waterhouse_-_Magic_Circle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Witchcraft","wikidata":"Q259745"},{"title":"Wood","blocks":[{"text":"Wood is a natural, lignocellulosic material derived primarily from the secondary xylem of trees and other woody plants, where it provides mechanical support and in the functional sapwood, conducts water and dissolved minerals. Being a natural material, it is characterized as an organic material – a natural composite of cellulosic fibers that are strong in tension and embedded in a matrix of lignin and hemicelluloses that resists compression."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/16_wood_samples.jpg/330px-16_wood_samples.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wood","wikidata":"Q287"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Witchcraft%3B_a_witch_and_a_devil_making_a_nail_with_which_to_Wellcome_V0025812EBL.jpg/500px-Witchcraft%3B_a_witch_and_a_devil_making_a_nail_with_which_to_Wellcome_V0025812EBL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Witchcraft%3B_a_witch_and_a_devil_making_a_nail_with_which_to_Wellcome_V0025812EBL.jpg/1280px-Witchcraft%3B_a_witch_and_a_devil_making_a_nail_with_which_to_Wellcome_V0025812EBL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Witchcraft%3B_a_witch_and_a_devil_making_a_nail_with_which_to_Wellcome_V0025812EBL.jpg/500px-Witchcraft%3B_a_witch_and_a_devil_making_a_nail_with_which_to_Wellcome_V0025812EBL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWitchcraft%3B_a_witch_and_a_devil_making_a_nail_with_which_to_Wellcome_V0025812EBL.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Heptameron_magic_circle.jpg/500px-Heptameron_magic_circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Heptameron_magic_circle.jpg/500px-Heptameron_magic_circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHeptameron_magic_circle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Baldung_Hexen_1508_kol.JPG/500px-Baldung_Hexen_1508_kol.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Baldung_Hexen_1508_kol.JPG/1280px-Baldung_Hexen_1508_kol.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Baldung_Hexen_1508_kol.JPG/500px-Baldung_Hexen_1508_kol.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Witches by Hans Baldung (woodcut), 1508","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABaldung_Hexen_1508_kol.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Hexenszene_1700.JPG/500px-Hexenszene_1700.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campa